<Base title="About" description="About TC Lee — IPC hardware BD, civil defense organizer, builder.">
  <div class="prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I'm TC Lee, based in Taipei. My work spans three domains that don't usually sit in the same room:
      industrial hardware, community resilience, and AI implementation.
    </p>

    <h2>Day job</h2>
    <p>
      I do business development for <a href="https://axiomtek.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Axiomtek</a>
      in European transportation and retail markets. Specifically: the embedded computers inside railway carriages,
      fleet vehicles, retail kiosks, and transit infrastructure. It's a niche world where hardware
      certification (EN50155, E-Mark, IP65) matters more than benchmark scores, and where a 10-year
      product lifecycle is normal. I attend InnoTrans, follow EU rail investment tenders, and work with
      equipment makers across Nordic and Western Europe.
    </p>

    <h2>Civil defense</h2>
    <p>
      I co-founded <strong>港湖民防團</strong> (Ganghu Civil Defense Team), a volunteer community
      organization in the Neihu/Ganghu district of Taipei. We run training in first aid (I'm EMT certified),
      emergency communications, and community preparedness. I'm also researching how ordinary people
      understand and respond to civil risk — what makes them act, and what keeps them from doing so.
    </p>
    <p>
      I've participated in Ukraine × Taiwan hybrid warfare workshops and follow civil defense developments
      internationally. This work is serious to me — not a hobby.
    </p>

    <h2>Building things</h2>
    <p>
      I'm self-taught: iOS developer, Shopify builder, occasional entrepreneur. These days I'm more
      focused on how AI changes the way small teams work — I lead AI implementation POCs at Axiomtek and
      use LLMs heavily in my BD and research workflows. I write about this on LinkedIn and here.
    </p>

    <h2>Writing</h2>
    <p>
      I've written in Chinese on <a href="https://tc-lee.medium.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Medium</a>
      since 2023 — iOS dev notes, startup observations. I've been posting in English on
      <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/t-c-lee" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
      since 2026. This site is the permanent home for writing I want to last.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Best reached on <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/t-c-lee" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
      For civil defense collaboration, find me through 港湖民防團.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
